WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.920
In the Yuan dynasty there was a famous master of calligraphy and painting, known to everyone as Zhao Mengfu.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:19.838
Zhao Mengfu believed in learning brushwork from the ancient masters, seeking new creative directions within a long tradition.

00:00:20.188 --> 00:00:29.332
In his quiet study, Zhao Mengfu lifted his brush and wrote; the big characters he produced looked vigorous and powerful.

00:00:29.682 --> 00:00:34.290
Beneath his brush there seemed to be a lively force of life.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.808
Then he picked up his painting brush and painted fine horses and landscapes, so vivid they seemed alive.

00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:47.902
People competed to collect his calligraphy and paintings, and earnestly imitated and studied his brush methods.

00:00:48.252 --> 00:00:55.044
In the history of both calligraphy and painting, Zhao Mengfu left a profound and important influence.

00:00:55.394 --> 00:00:59.690
Hundreds of years have passed, and his name still shines brightly.

